      "place": "Charles Bridge, Prague (Czech Republic)",
      "kind": "real",
      "kept": [
        "Charles Bridge between the Mala Strana and Old Town bridge towers",
        "Kampa island cut off by the Certovka channel, with its footbridge",
        "Old Town water tower beside the bridgehead",
        "Old Town Square with the Old Town Hall, the Jan Hus memorial and the Tyn church",
        "St. Nicholas church on the Mala Strana square and the Petrin slope"
      ],
      "simplified": [
        "Map rotated: the Vltava runs west-east, Mala Strana is north, Old Town south",
        "The river and every district are compressed to game scale",
        "A modern road bridge stands east of Charles Bridge to give a second crossing",
        "The Prague Castle hill is suggested only by the forested Petrin corner"
      ]
    },
